the aftermath of an attack by Syrian  government forces and their Russian  allies in Eid Lib province the attack  happened hours before a Russian and  Turkish brokered ceasefire was due to  come into effect volunteer white helmet  paramedics were there within minutes to  do what they've done thousands of times  during the war tried to save the lives  of civilians there have been several  airstrikes on two different cities he  went to the sites and while we were  helping people there were more  airstrikes for sure there are people  trapped under the rubble we're still  searching for survivors  omne wrap was one of several villages  hit by Russian and Syrian government  forces in the last 24 hours  this grandfather is burying four out of  his five granddaughters I wasn't here  when the airstrikes happened but I was  told my granddaughter's had been killed  when we came we found their bodies their  parents are in the hospital having  surgery only one three-month-old baby  survived more than 1,300 civilians have  been killed since the government  launched its offensive to retake Italy  province in 2018 this territory is the  last stronghold of groups opposed to  President Bashar al-assad Russia which  supports Assad and Turkey which backs  the rebels announced a ceasefire on  Thursday which has now come into effect  but it was too late  for these children early on the servitor  mafia - what the airstrike led to a  massacre most the victims are children  these are the dead bodies I won the  world feed these children look at the  crimes of Bashar al-assad last August  Russia and Turkey agreed a de-escalation  zone in Italy province but attacks  continued and many here don't believe  this ceasefire will last either  Victoria Gaytan be al-jazeera
 

